   "subject": "Re: Summary (UD) produces results in different measurement units (km2 and hectares)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I think <span>units=FALSE</span> makes sense if users are doing a batch analysis, while <span>units=TRUE</span> makes sense for users analyzing individuals interactively on the command line. I&#39;m not sure which use case is more common, but the effort to type <span>units=TRUE</span> ten times on the command line is more than the effort to type <span>units=FALSE</span> one time in an R script.<br><br>Best,<br>Chris</div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
